# Compliance Rules

See root `AGENTS.md` §"Key compliance facts" for the full list.

## Hard rules

- VAT rates are NEVER hardcoded in component files. Always import `getFoodVatRate`
  from `packages/compliance/src/vat.ts`.
- DAC7 thresholds are NEVER hardcoded. Always import `DAC7_THRESHOLDS` from
  `packages/compliance/src/vat.ts`.
- The 14 EU allergens are NEVER hardcoded as string arrays in components. Always
  import `EU_ALLERGENS_14` from `packages/compliance/src/allergens.ts`.
- Every compliance-sensitive function must have a `// COMPLIANCE-REVIEW:` comment
  explaining what a lawyer needs to verify before it goes live.
- "Sold by [Seller Name]" must appear as a persistent, non-decorative element on
  every product card and cart line (DSA Art. 30(7)).
- AllergenBadge must always include an `aria-label` — never rely on colour or
  icon alone (WCAG 1.4.1).

## DSA suspension timing

DAC7 and DSA share the same onboarding data collection but have DIFFERENT
suspension clocks. Do not let the more lenient DAC7 grace period (~60 days)
leak into DSA-covered enforcement (which requires *swift* suspension).
Implement as two separate flags/timers.
